---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
    title="Editorial Policy | SaveTikFast"
    description="How SaveTikFast researches, writes, reviews, updates, and separates advertising from its educational guides and creator resources."
    pageType="page"
>
    <main class="policy">
        <article>
            <p class="eyebrow">SaveTikFast standards</p>
            <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
            <p class="updated">Last updated: November 9, 2026</p>

            <h2>Purpose</h2>
            <p>Our articles help readers make informed decisions about creator workflows, public-link archiving, audio formatting, digital rights, and online privacy. Every guide is written to be practical and accurate on its own, even when a reader does not use our web utilities.</p>

            <h2>How we select and test topics</h2>
            <p>We publish guides only when we can answer a real technical or workflow question with verifiable steps across iOS, Android, macOS, and Windows browsers. We prioritize topics where context matters: creator permissions, proper attribution, audio/video codecs, troubleshooting browser downloads, and protecting personal privacy. We do not publish thin doorway pages solely to target search keywords.</p>

            <h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
            <p>Browser behaviors, mobile operating systems, and social platform features evolve regularly. We test workflows directly, state technical limitations clearly, avoid unrealistic guarantees, and revise or retire outdated guides. Readers can report an inaccuracy at <a href="mailto:support@savetik-fast.xyz">support@savetik-fast.xyz</a>.</p>

            <h2>Originality</h2>
            <p>All guides on SaveTikFast are written and reviewed internally for our readers. Where a workflow depends on creator permission, platform terms, or local copyright regulations, we highlight those requirements explicitly rather than offering shortcuts as universal legal advice.</p>

            <h2>Advertising &amp; commercial independence</h2>
            <p>SaveTikFast is free to use and supported by third-party display advertising (such as Google AdSense) on eligible tool and editorial pages. Advertisements are visually distinct from editorial content and download controls, never appear on legal or error pages, and never influence our technical recommendations or conclusions.</p>

            <h2>Responsible use</h2>
            <p>We support lawful personal use, accessibility, and respect for original creators. Our editorial content never encourages copyright infringement, unauthorized commercial redistribution, or attempts to bypass privacy controls on restricted accounts.</p>
        </article>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    .policy { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3.5rem 20px; }
    article { background: var(--glass); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.8; }
    :global([data-theme="light"]) article { background: #ffffff; box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05); }
    .eyebrow { color: var(--secondary); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; font-size: .8rem; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem); margin: .4rem 0; }
    .updated { color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    h2 { color: var(--secondary); margin: 2rem 0 .7rem; font-size: 1.45rem; }
    p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    a { color: var(--secondary); }
</style>
